# Local, unmerged patch against FIPS 2ba790b (0.6.0-dev).
#
# Per-peer forwarding + runtime admission + local link price.
#
# (a) admission:
#   - Node.acl_overrides: HashMap<NodeAddr, bool>
#   - control set_admission {npub, action: allow|deny|clear}
#   - fipsctl admission <peer> allow|deny|clear
#   - authorize_peer checks the override before the file ACL
#
# (b) forwarding:
#   - Node.forwarding_blocked: HashSet<NodeAddr>
#   - control set_forwarding {npub, allow}
#   - fipsctl set-forwarding <peer> allow|block
#   - drop_policy_blocked_{packets,bytes} + policy_blocked_by_peer
#   - transit drop in handle_session_datagram
#
# (c) price:
#   - Node.link_prices: HashMap<NodeAddr, f64>
#   - cost = link_cost * (1 + price) at every peer_costs construction
#   - control set_price {npub, price|null}
#   - fipsctl set-price <peer> <price|clear>
#   - a price change forces one reevaluation on the next tick; the tree's
#     hysteresis and hold-down still apply
#
# A blocked peer keeps its link, Noise session and local delivery (the payment
# lane). Only datagrams it sends to a third party are not forwarded.
#
# DO NOT submit this to jmcorgan/fips. It is a local experiment patch; any
# upstream conversation goes out of band via Signal after reproducible results,
# per AGENTS.md.
#
